[MEDIUM]
Q: What is the preorder traversal of the BST built by inserting 50, 30, 70, 20, 40, 60 in that order?
A) 50 30 20 40 70 60
B) 20 30 40 50 60 70
C) 20 40 30 60 70 50
D) 50 30 70 20 40 60
ANSWER: A
HINT: Preorder = Root, Left subtree, Right subtree. First draw the tree.
EXPLAIN: Tree: 50 with left 30 (children 20, 40) and right 70 (left child 60). Preorder: 50 30 20 40 70 60.

[MEDIUM]
Q: What is the output of this program?
CODE java
public class Main {
    static class Node {
        int v; Node l, r;
        Node(int v, Node l, Node r) { this.v = v; this.l = l; this.r = r; }
    }
    static int height(Node n) {
        if (n == null) return 0;
        return 1 + Math.max(height(n.l), height(n.r));
    }
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Node t = new Node(1,
                new Node(2, new Node(4, null, null), null),
                new Node(3, null, new Node(5, null, new Node(6, null, null))));
        System.out.println(height(t));
    }
}
END
A) 3
B) 4
C) 5
D) 6
ANSWER: B
HINT: Here height counts nodes on the longest root-to-leaf path. Find that path first.
EXPLAIN: The longest path is 1 -> 3 -> 5 -> 6, which has 4 nodes.

[MEDIUM]
Q: In an array-based binary heap (index starting at 0), what are the indices of the children of the node at index i?
A) 2i and 2i + 1
B) 2i + 1 and 2i + 2
C) i + 1 and i + 2
D) i/2 and i/2 + 1
ANSWER: B
HINT: The root is at index 0 and its children must be at 1 and 2.
EXPLAIN: With 0-based indexing, left = 2i + 1 and right = 2i + 2; the parent is (i - 1) / 2.

[HARD]
Q: An AVL tree contains the keys 10, 20 (inserted in that order). Key 30 is inserted next. Which rotation restores balance, and which key becomes the root?
A) Right rotation; root 10
B) Left rotation; root 20
C) Left-Right rotation; root 30
D) No rotation needed; root 10
ANSWER: B
HINT: The imbalance is on the right side of the right child (RR case).
EXPLAIN: 10 -> 20 -> 30 is a right-right chain; a single left rotation at 10 makes 20 the root with children 10 and 30.

[HARD]
Q: What is the output of this program?
CODE java
public class Main {
    static int count(int n) {
        if (n <= 1) return 1;
        int total = 0;
        for (int root = 1; root <= n; root++) {
            total += count(root - 1) * count(n - root);
        }
        return total;
    }
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        System.out.println(count(4));
    }
}
END
A) 14
B) 16
C) 24
D) 10
ANSWER: A
HINT: Each value can be the root; multiply the number of possible left and right subtrees. This computes Catalan numbers.
EXPLAIN: It counts structurally different BSTs on 4 keys: C(4) = 14.

